; THE FEN EDGE — a transitional cell (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul).
;
; ⚠️ IT IS ALMOST EMPTY AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. Everything the player sees here — the ground,
; its elevation, its collision, the vegetation on it and the road across it — is authored in
; data/regions/EmberCrown.tres and built at load: the terrain mesh from the region heightfield,
; the ecology from the cell's biome scatter profile, the route from its path segments. A
; transitional cell costs one terrain draw and a handful of MultiMesh draws, which is what makes
; making the world five times larger cheaper per square metre rather than more expensive.
;
; Sodden dead ground west of the wharf. A causeway crosses the marsh and stops. No loot, no
; encounter marker, no NPC, no map pin.
;
; ⚠️ THE DROWNED MARKER, AND WHY A CELL WITH "NOTHING TO FIND" HAS SIX NODES IN IT NOW.
;
; This causeway runs out into the marsh and stops. It stopped at nothing at all, which is a
; different thing from being empty: a road is a promise, and a strong visible path that leads to
; literally no acknowledgement teaches the player that following one is not worth the walk. Once
; they have learned that, every road in the realm is worth less.
;
; So the end of the causeway is a PLACE without being a REWARD. Two pillars and a broken wall stand
; half in the water where something used to be - the far end of a crossing the fen took back - and
; the ground under them is the one rise on this side, so a player who walks out here is looking back
; across open water at Hollowreach's wharf and tower. There is no loot, no interactable, no enemy,
; no map pin and no dialogue. Curiosity is answered with a view and a story, and nothing else.
;
; ⚠️ DO NOT ADD A CHEST HERE. The moment a dead end pays out, every dead end has to.

; ⚠️ DO NOT FILL THIS IN. If a beat wants to happen here, the honest question is whether the realm
; needs another beat or whether this stretch is doing its job.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. ⚠️ AND THE agent_* DIMS DID NOT FOLLOW. On the 0.25 grid 1.75 and
; 0.5 were whole voxels; on this one they are not, so every bake quantised them and warned. The
; values below are the QUANTISED ones, so the file now says what the bake does: agent_height and
; agent_radius CEIL to a voxel (cell_height / cell_size), agent_max_climb FLOORS to cell_height.
; ⚠️ They encode this grid — change cell_size or cell_height and recompute all three with it.
; ⚠️ prp_ruin_pillar STANDS UP - the 4 m box is the pillar, not a fallen one lying on its side.
